under the MIT License. The upstream license is preserved in LICENSE.

Ryoku calls this port Nomarchy to distinguish the modified work from Omarchy.
The port retains the upstream bar, panels, widgets, menus, plugin host,
notification presentation, OSD, reminders, media and battery integrations.

Ryoku adaptations include:

- all output, workspace, window, focus and keyboard-layout operations use the
  neutral Ryoku window-manager contract;
- shared QML primitives use Ryoku tokens and output state;
- the resident Ryoku notification server feeds Nomarchy's history and toast UI;
- Ryogami owns wallpaper selection and ryoshot/Recorder own capture;
- Ryoku owns lock, clipboard, policy authentication, idle inhibition,
  night-light and update flows;
- the Agents panel keeps upstream usage and extension surfaces, while account
  controls stay hidden when the platform account capability reports unavailable;
- the Agents launch action opens Ryoku Ask and the duplicate starter-prompt
  surface is omitted;
- third-party plugins are fail-closed behind `ryoku wm compat <plugin-dir>`;
- state and data paths honor XDG_STATE_HOME and XDG_DATA_HOME;
- Bar Studio exposes Nomarchy themes and plugin controls;
- every QML file imports `QtQuick 6.11`, because Qt 6.12's new QtQuick `Color`
  singleton shadows the shell's own `Color` (QTBUG-151278).

